-- What's new: the latest versions' notes for the settings panel.
-- GENERATED by tools/changelog2lua.js from CHANGELOG.md; do not edit by hand.
local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.0", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nFlareUI now draws its own nameplates. Every kind of unit gets its own look: enemy players and NPCs, friendly players and NPCs, and minor mobs with pets and totems. Open-world PvP gets full plates, quest givers get a clean name, and you can tweak every one of them with a live preview at your side. The chat also learned a few tricks, and unit frames can show the name above the frame.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffChat:|r a popped-out chat window now fades on its own. It comes back for its own messages only, not for every line in every window.\n• |cffffffffVisibility Never:|r a frame set to Never no longer shows tooltips when you point where it is.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menus:|r the |cffffffffMounts|r catalog is now |cffffffffCollections|r, with your mounts and your toys.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r FlareUI's own nameplates, with a setup for each unit type.\n• |cffffffffName Above Plates:|r the name above any unit frame, so the bars stay clean.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r fade old lines one by one, and quiet loot and skill-ups.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates (new page, off)|r\n• First in the Combat list. A /reload turns it on or off.\n• |cffffffffUnit types|r, each with its own setup: |cffffffffEnemy Player|r, |cffffffffEnemy NPC|r, |cffffffffFriendly Player|r, |cffffffffFriendly NPC|r and |cffffffffMinor|r (minor mobs, pets, totems and guardians).\n• |cffffffffPresets|r for each unit: |cffffffffFull|r, |cffffffffSimple|r, |cffffffffMinimal|r, |cffffffffName Only|r. Change any setting and it becomes that unit's own Custom.\n      - Friendly players and NPCs start on Name Only.\n• |cffffffffLive Preview|r beside the settings, and |cffffffffTest in Game|r to put the look on the plates around you.\n• |cffffffffPlate:|r size, |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r, |cffffffffBar Texture|r, |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffLevel|r, |cffffffffBar Effects|r, |cffffffffColour By|r, |cffffffffHealth Text|r.\n      - |cffffffffName Only Mode|r: just the name, with |cffffffffName Only Size|r.\n      - |cffffffffShow Plates in Combat|r: picked units leave Name Only in a fight.\n• |cffffffffExtras:|r\n      - Icons: |cffffffffElite & Rare|r, |cffffffffCombo Points|r, |cffffffffQuest Objective|r, |cffffffffQuest Progress|r.\n      - Threat: |cffffffffColour by Threat|r, |cffffffffRole|r, |cffffffffThreat Glow|r, |cffffffffAggro Flash|r, |cffffffffThreat Scale|r, |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r.\n      - Colours: |cffffffffExecute Range|r, |cffffffffColour Mob Types|r, |cffffffffParty Colour|r, |cffffffffRaid Colour|r.\n• |cffffffffCast Bar:|r icon, timer and target, |cffffffffKick Ready Colour|r, |cffffffffKick Ready Mark|r, |cffffffffFlash When Targeted|r, |cffffffffHighlight Important Casts|r.\n• |cffffffffAuras:|r buffs, debuffs, |cffffffffDefensives|r and |cffffffffCrowd Control|r, each with size and count.\n• |cffffffffTargeting|r (all plates): target and non-target scale and opacity, |cffffffffOut of Range|r and |cffffffffOut of Sight|r fading, target |cffffffffArrow|r, |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffBar Colour|r, |cffffffffOuter Glow|r and |cffffffffFocus Colour|r.\n• |cffffffffVisibility|r (all plates):\n      - Which enemies and friends get a plate, |cffffffffStacking|r, |cffffffffKeep Target on Screen|r, |cffffffffClick-Through|r.\n      - |cffffffffName Only While Unattackable|r (off): enemy NPCs you can't attack yet show only their name.\n      - The game's names over heads: |cffffffffNPC Names|r, |cffffffffPlayer Names|r, |cffffffffMinion Names|r.\n• |cffffffffNameplate Colours|r in FlareUI's colour window, and a Fonts tab.\n• |cffffd100/fui plates|r prints what the module sees, for bug reports.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffName Above Plates|r (Off), in the Text section in Edit Mode: First Name or Full Name above the frame, on the left, centre or right.\n      - Auras and a cast bar above the frame move up to make room.\n      - On the player, target, focus, pet, target of target, target of focus, party, boss and flag carrier frames. Not on Forever Style, which has its name box.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffOnly Chat Messages|r: a new Visibility choice. Only lines people write bring the chat back; loot, skill-ups and XP stay quiet.\n• |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r (off), under Fading in Edit Mode: lines fade one by one, oldest first. Pointing at the chat or typing brings them back.\n\n|cffe6cc99Visibility|r\n• |cffffffffNot in a Capital City|r: last on every Visibility list, the reverse of In a Capital City.\n• |cffffffffFade Delay|r goes up to 1 minute (chat and meter).\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menus|r\n• |cffffffffCollections|r catalog: mounts, then toys.\n• Small titles split the catalog's lists: Mounts and Toys, Spells and Pet Spells, Target and World Markers, General and Character Macros, Professions and Profession Spells.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffXP Bar:|r |cffffffffShow Tooltip|r (off) brings the bar's tooltip back.\n• |cffffd100/fui buff|r opens the Buff Reminders settings.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Settings text: clearer descriptions and tips, using the options' real names.\n• Faster in several places: nameplate colours, buff reminder aura checks, resource bar text and the heal bars on party frames.\n• French: the 6.14 phrases. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: the mouse wheel scrolls the chat again, also when the game's own chat scroll setting is off." },
    { version = "6.14", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nA new page joins the Combat list: |cffffffffCooldowns|r, built by brudi, brings FlareUI's look and a few handy extras to Blizzard's Cooldown Manager. Your backpack can now sort itself into rows, and the Edit Mode windows finally stay where you put them.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r moved from Action Bars to the new |cffffffffCooldowns|r page. If it was on, Cooldowns is on too.\n• |cffffffffCategory Filters|r is now a choice in |cffffffffBag View|r (Bags & Looting › Bag Window). If you had filters on, you get Category Filters: the buttons by the search box when there's room, the drawer otherwise.\n• |cffffffffXP Bar:|r |cffffffffFlareUI XP Bar|r is now called |cffffffffBar Style|r, and its tooltip is gone. It covered the bar's own text.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r settings windows no longer jump next to the frame you click. They open at the top right, then wherever you last dragged one.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffCooldowns:|r Blizzard's Cooldown Manager in FlareUI's style. By brudi.\n• |cffffffffBag View:|r the combined backpack sorted into category rows. By andrzejskibinski.\n• |cffffffffIn a Capital City:|r a new Visibility condition on every frame.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldowns (new page, off)|r\n• First in the Combat list. It changes Blizzard's own Cooldown Manager bars.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager|r section:\n      - |cffffffffEnable Blizzard Cooldown Manager|r: the same switch as in the game's options.\n      - |cffffffffAdvanced Cooldown Settings|r: opens Blizzard's window where you pick what each bar tracks.\n• |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r (off): Tracked Bars like FlareUI's cast bars, icons with FlareUI's borders.\n• |cffffffffBar Colour|r: the Tracked Bars' colour, in FlareUI's colour window.\n• Icons (all off):\n      - |cffffffffShow Keybind Text|r: your keybinds on the Essential and Utility icons.\n      - |cffffffffShow Button Presses|r: an icon lights up while you hold its key.\n      - |cffffffffSoften Active Overlay|r: a faint swipe over a running effect, so you can see the icon.\n      - |cffffffffShow Cooldown During Effect|r: the ability's own cooldown in the icon's corner.\n• Fonts tab: |cffffffffKeybinds|r, |cffffffffCounts|r, |cffffffffCooldown Numbers|r and |cffffffffBar Text|r.\n• Edit Mode, on each Cooldown Manager bar:\n      - |cffffffffGrowth|r (Blizzard): Tracked Buffs and Tracked Bars packed together, growing right, left, down, up or from the middle.\n      - |cffffffffIcon Shape|r (Square): Square or Rectangle.\n      - |cffffffffFading|r, as on every other frame.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• |cffffffffBag View|r (All Items), in Bags & Looting › Bag Window:\n      - |cffffffffCategory Filters|r: the filter buttons, as before.\n      - |cffffffffCategory Rows|r: the combined backpack in sections: Quest Items, Equipment, Materials, Consumables, Junk and Other.\n      - |cffffffffCategory Rows + Sets|r: a section for each equipment set too.\n• The |cffffffff+|r button (more bag space) sits at the left end of the gold bar.\n\n|cffe6cc99Visibility|r\n• |cffffffffIn a Capital City|r: last on every Visibility list. Shows the frame in Stormwind, Ironforge, Darnassus, Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff and Undercity.\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• The FlareUI layout code (About page and setup tour) has the new layout.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Settings window: a little taller, so every page fits in the list.\n• Minimap › Addon Buttons: the preview follows |cffffffffDrawer Button Size|r, |cffffffffFlareUI Minimap Button|r and |cffffffffDrawer Style|r as you change them. By parchinskiy.\n• XP Bar settings: |cffffffffBar Texture|r, |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffSeparators|r and |cffffffffPick Your Colours|r sit right under |cffffffffBar Style|r.\n• French: the 6.13 phrases. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Custom fonts: text drawn before its font loaded no longer stays blank after login (the Info Bar, keybinds and more).\n• Chat: the |cffffffffCopy Chat|r button opens Copy Chat again.\n• Quest Tracker: a plain \"Ready for turn-in\" line is grey, as on Blizzard's tracker.\n• Quest Tracker on Visibility |cffffffffNever|r: no more tooltips or clicks where it was.\n• Buff Reminders: the food reminder remembers food you eat anywhere, also from /use macros.\n• Fake CM: its Visibility names were one place off." },
    { version = "6.13", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new art files.\n\nA huge thank-you to parchinskiy, a great collaborator who tracked down and fixed the hardest bug we've had so far: the bags breaking your clicks after a bank visit. This patch is also the big settings clean-up: every page and Edit Mode window got the same order, the same words and the same rules, and the unit frames now offer the same options in every style.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffVendor|r options moved to |cffffffffBags & Looting|r, and now follow that page's switch. If Bags & Looting is off, turn it on to keep Auto Sell Junk, Auto Repair and the rest.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r the new |cffffffffColour Scheme|r starts at |cffffffffFlareUI|r: softer, bronze-toned colours on the FlareUI and Modern styles. Pick |cffffffffBlizzard|r for the old colours.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r new installs start with the |cffffffffModern|r style. Your current style stays as it is.\n• |cffffffffNames on unit frames:|r outside Forever Style, the name is now a pick in |cffffffffHealth Text|r only. If you had |cffffffffShow Name|r off, the name is back: untick it in Health Text.\n• |cffffffffParty (Classic) and boss frames:|r |cffffffffHealth Text|r and |cffffffffPower Text|r are now the Left / Centre / Right picker. Your old choice carries over.\n• |cffffffffGryphons:|r the |cffffffffSame as Action Bar 1|r Visibility choice is gone. Gryphons that used it now join bar 1's fade group, or copy its Visibility.\n• |cffffffffMinimap drawer:|r |cffffffffAddons in the Drawer: None|r now keeps every addon button on the minimap's edge. |cffffffffDrawer Style: Off|r turns the drawer off. If you had None, your drawer is now set to Off.\n• |cffffffffBar textures|r renamed: FlareUI Forever is |cffffffffFlareUI Dark|r, FlareUI Forever (Light) is |cffffffffFlareUI Light|r. Your picks carry over.\n• |cffffffffAura Swipe|r and |cffffffffAura Timer|r left the Buffs and Debuffs Edit Mode windows: set them in Settings › Buffs & Debuffs. The totems' are in Buffs & Debuffs › |cffffffffTotems|r.\n• |cffffffffShields|r over health bars are lighter (40%, was 75%), so the health under them shows.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffSettings clean-up:|r dropdowns, then sliders, then switches everywhere; one word for each idea; fewer, clearer sections.\n• |cffffffffUnit frame parity:|r the same options on every frame and style where they make sense.\n• |cffffffffChat and Meters:|r the FlareUI |cffffffffFrame Style|r.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed:|r square or round icons with a border in the item's quality colour.\n• |cffffffffValues on Mouseover:|r health and power numbers only while you point at a frame, as Blizzard's option.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r (off), in each frame's Text section in Edit Mode: health and power numbers show only while you point at the frame. On every unit frame, party, raid, boss and flag carrier frame.\n• |cffffffffLevel Disc Size|r (100%), in each frame's Text section, FlareUI and Forever Style, with |cffffffffShow Level|r on. It replaces the one slider in Settings. By SSyl.\n• |cffffffffShow Combat Text|r (off), player and pet, FlareUI and Forever Style: Blizzard's hit and heal numbers on the portrait. Its font is in Unit Frames › Fonts › |cffffffffCombat Text|r.\n• |cffffffffPortrait Scale|r (100%) is back on FlareUI Style frames, now on party, boss and flag carrier frames too.\n• |cffffffffShow Weapon Enchants|r (on), player frame: the enchants follow |cffffffffHide Buffs|r too.\n• |cffffffffCombo Points|r is one dropdown in every style: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffClassic|r (the gems) or |cffffffffModern|r (a bar). Forever Style's gems can now be turned off.\n• Focus frame: |cffffffffLeader|r, |cffffffffPvP Flag|r and |cffffffffQuest Objective|r icons, as on the target frame.\n• Target and focus: |cffffffffDispel Highlight|r (Off), for a friendly unit you can dispel.\n• Pet frame: |cffffffffRange Check|r (off).\n• Boss frames: |cffffffffHigh Level Skull|r (on), FlareUI and Forever Style.\n• Flag carrier frames: |cffffffffClass Colours|r.\n• Party, boss and flag carrier cast bars: their own |cffffffffBackground|r; boss and flag carriers also get |cffffffffPosition|r (Above or Below). Cast bar |cffffffffHeight|r goes up to 40 on every frame.\n• Main Tanks: |cffffffffTarget Frame Width|r and |cffffffffTarget Frame Height|r for Tank Targets (Auto follows the tank's frame).\n• Player Cast Bar: |cffffffffShow Speed|r and |cffffffffHide Speed|r in its Fading.\n• Mirror Bars has a description.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffFrame Style|r (Modern): |cffffffffFlareUI|r puts the quest tracker's look on the chat.\n• |cffffffffWhisper Sound|r (Off): Raid Warning, Alarm or Whisper. The speaker button plays it.\n• Middle-click a whisper tab to close it.\n• |cffffffffIcons|r dropdown: |cffffffffItem and Spell Icons|r, |cffffffffRace Icons|r, |cffffffffClass Icons|r (were three switches).\n• |cffffffffNotifications|r section: |cffffffffTab Glow|r and |cffffffffWhisper Sound|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• |cffffffffFrame Style|r (Modern), as on the chat.\n• |cffffffffBar Texture|r (Blizzard).\n• |cffffffffThreat Window|r: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffSeparate Window|r or |cffffffffIn the Meter in Combat|r (were two switches).\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffColour Scheme|r: |cffffffffBlizzard|r or |cffffffffFlareUI|r (default).\n• |cffffffffHeader Buttons|r: |cffffffffFilter|r, |cffffffffSort|r, |cffffffffAuto Accept|r and |cffffffffAuto Turn-In|r box buttons on the header.\n• |cffffffffHide Scroll Bar|r (off).\n• |cffffffffAuto Minimize|r dropdown: |cffffffffIn Instances|r, |cffffffffIn Combat|r, |cffffffffOn Flight Paths|r (new).\n• |cffffffffShow Untracked Quests|r works without Zone Headings: the untracked ones come after your tracked quests.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed|r is now |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffSquare Icons|r or |cffffffffRound Icons|r. Each icon has a border in the item's quality colour.\n• Loot Feed: |cffffffffScale|r in its Edit Mode window.\n• |cffffffffSkin Item Slots|r: |cffffffffColour by Rarity|r is back, under a line in the dropdown (on).\n\n|cffe6cc99Buffs & Debuffs|r\n• |cffffffffAura Filters|r (was Hide Auras): each spell can be |cffffffffHide|r or |cffffffffShow|r. Shown spells get their own row and skip the other filters.\n• |cffffffffTotems|r section: |cffffffffAura Swipe|r and |cffffffffAura Timer|r for your totems.\n• |cffffffffNever|r in the Visibility of the buff and debuff frames.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• A reminder waits while its spell is on cooldown (Fear Ward).\n• Food: a click eats the food that last gave you Well Fed.\n• |cffffffffUpkeep|r dropdown (was six switches), with |cffffffffWeapon Oil / Stone|r in it.\n• |cffffffffIcon Alerts|r dropdown in Edit Mode: |cffffffffGlow When Missing|r, |cffffffffGlow When Running Out|r, |cffffffffTime Left|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffMinimap Icons|r section: one |cffffffffIcons|r dropdown (|cffffffffSundial|r, |cffffffffGroup Finder|r, |cffffffffVehicle Exit|r, |cffffffffDurability Warning|r) and |cffffffffReset Minimap Icons|r.\n• Info Bar: |cffffffffExperience|r.\n• Happy Camper and Lore Forever buttons sit in the minimap's button row.\n• The day/night sundial lights up under your mouse and has a tooltip. By parchinskiy.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• Gryphons: |cffffffffScale|r in each gryphon's Edit Mode window.\n• XP Bar: |cffffffffBar Texture|r and |cffffffffBorder|r are in Settings › Action Bars › XP Bar (were in Edit Mode).\n\n|cffe6cc99Everywhere|r\n• |cffffffffNever|r in every Edit Mode Visibility, first in the list. A unit frame on Never takes no clicks.\n• Sound dropdowns have a speaker button that plays the sound.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings|r\n• Every page and Edit Mode window: dropdowns first, then sliders, then switches.\n• Options that depend on another one sit in line and grey out, no longer indented.\n• Names, one word per idea:\n      - |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r (was Frame Opacity), |cffffffffScale|r for sizes in %, |cffffffffMax Buffs|r and |cffffffffMax Debuffs|r (were Buff Amount and Debuff Amount), |cffffffffBorder|r on cast bars (was Border Texture), |cffffffffCentre|r, |cffffffffOff|r first in every list.\n      - |cffffffffSync Blizzard UI|r, |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stances|r, |cffffffffThreat Text|r (was Show Threat, now in the Text section), |cffffffffAt the Cursor|r (Tooltips, was Mouseover), |cffffffffShow My Frame in a Party / Raid|r (were Hide Player Frame).\n      - Fonts: |cffffffffCounts|r, |cffffffffMacro Text|r, |cffffffffSpell Timer|r.\n      - Section names: |cffffffffBars|r, |cffffffffButtons|r, |cffffffffSpell Behaviour|r, |cffffffffFrames|r, |cffffffffController|r, |cffffffffConsumables|r, |cffffffffAuras|r and |cffffffffOrdering|r.\n      - Unit frame aura places read |cffffffffAbove the Frame|r, |cffffffffBelow the Frame, Left|r and so on.\n      - Quest Tracker style |cffffffffCustom|r is |cffffffffModern|r; Unit Frames |cffffffffAddon Style|r is |cffffffffModern Style|r; borders |cffffffffFlareUI Thin|r and |cffffffffFlareUI Thick|r.\n• Quality of Life's |cffffffffInterface|r tab is now |cffffffffExtras|r.\n• Minimap sections: |cffffffffLook|r, |cffffffffInfo Bar|r, |cffffffffTweaks|r, |cffffffffMinimap Icons|r, |cffffffffAddon Buttons|r.\n• Quest Tracker tabs: |cffffffffFrame|r, |cffffffffBehaviour|r, |cffffffffFonts|r; |cffffffffHeader Buttons|r moved to Frame.\n• Buff Reminders: the |cffffffffAlerts|r tab joined |cffffffffWhen and Where|r.\n• Portrait, Flip Portrait and Mirror Bars moved to each frame's |cffffffffLook|r section in Edit Mode.\n• Simple Pet Frame, Simple Target of Target and Level Disc Size are hidden in Modern Style, where they do nothing.\n• Edit Mode rows that do nothing on a Fake Cooldown Manager bar are hidden there.\n• Aura sizes: 8 to 48 on every frame (raid tiles 8 to 30).\n• Meters: |cffffffffMatch Chat Size|r and the Meter Tab rows grey out with Chat off, instead of hiding.\n• |cffffffffOpen Flight Map at Once|r moved to Map & Mail.\n\n|cffe6cc99Look|r\n• One bronze for the ring styles' frames, rings and boss dragons, and for the minimap's Blizzard art.\n• Warmer colours across the settings, tooltips and windows; aura borders a lighter bronze.\n• Bronze header icons on the chat, meters and loot rolls are darker.\n• Quest Tracker: a plain \"Ready for turn-in\" line is grey, as Blizzard's.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffBags:|r after a bank visit, right-clicks on items stopped working (Cozy Sleeping Bag, bank tabs). The keyring and crafting bag now use Blizzard's own clicks. By parchinskiy.\n• Gryphons faded with action bar 1 whatever their Visibility said.\n• Raid frames: Width and Height only moved the gaps with Tank Targets on.\n• Chat: an error when switching tabs in a fight; an error in the tab bar under combat restrictions.\n• Edit Mode: an error with hidden auras under restrictions.\n• Minimap FlareUI Thin and Thick borders: the map's corners now follow the border's angled corners.\n• Minimap drawer: takes buttons from EnhanceQoL and HidingBar. By AreChen.\n• Info Bar dividers stay one pixel wide at any UI scale. By Celbrund.\n• Small action buttons (stance, pet, possess, totem): thinner border, no overlap. By Celbrund.\n• Radial Menu: Sub-Radials reset on close kept the last button's name and icon.\n• Radial emote labels in Russian lost their first letter.\n• Keybinds sometimes missing at the first login.\n• The layout restore box: Not Now keeps your layout, and a restore that didn't stick isn't offered again.\n• Details! chat embed fits FlareUI's chat window.\n• Quest Tracker: lines kept their old colours after a Colour Scheme switch.\n• Totem Bar Scale showed with Action Bars off.\n\n|cffffd100Translations|r\n• |cffffffffHungarian|r, new. By Xentinus. Loot roll buttons use FlareUI's Need, Greed, Pass and Transmog words where your language has them.\n• French: the 6.12 phrases. By Brainc3ll." },
    { version = "6.12", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\nA huge thank-you to AreChen for the Chinese translations and for all the help this week. This patch started as a few fixes and then kept growing: a new quest tracker look, minimap icons you can move around the edge, health colours, bar text in the order you pick, and a pile of fixes from your Discord reports.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r the new |cffffffffFrame Style|r starts at |cffffffffFlareUI|r: Blizzard's title and zone strips on FlareUI's frame, with a thicker border. Pick |cffffffffCustom|r for the old look.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker fonts|r (only if you never set them): Header 12, Quest Names 11, Objectives 10 (were 13, 12 and 11).\n• |cffffffffHide Buffs|r now starts at |cffffffffOff|r on every frame, as on Blizzard's frames. Buffs without a timer show again: tracking, mounts, Plainsrunning and so on. To hide them, set |cffffffffHide Buffs|r in the frame's Edit Mode settings.\n• |cffffffffChat, Meters and Quest Tracker:|r |cffffffffFrame Opacity|r starts at 75% (was 60%), if you never changed it.\n• |cffffffffBar Text:|r if 6.11 turned your health text into \"% / Value\", untick both and tick them again in the order you want.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffBar Text:|r numbers show in the order you tick them, and the menu numbers your ticks.\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r move the sundial and the other edge icons around the map, and pick a new |cffffffffBorder|r.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r |cffffffffFrame Style|r, |cffffffffQuest Buttons|r and Blizzard's glows.\n• |cffffffffTint Health:|r health bars that turn red when low, or shift from green to red.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffTint Health|r (Off), in each frame's Behaviour section in Edit Mode:\n      - |cffffffffOn Low Health:|r the bar turns red under 30%.\n      - |cffffffffBy Health:|r the bar goes from green to yellow to red.\n      - On every unit frame, party, raid, boss and flag carrier frame, and the Resource Bars' health bar.\n      - It replaces the Resource Bars' |cffffffffLow Health Colour|r switch. Your setting carries over.\n• Player frame: |cffffffffGCD Spark|r (off), after |cffffffffFive-Second Rule|r.\n• Player frame: |cffffffffDispel Highlight|r (off), in Edit Mode › Auras: the frame lights up in the colour of a debuff you can remove.\n• Debuff icons 18 px and bigger show the debuff's type (Magic, Curse, Poison, Disease) in their top right corner.\n• Party and raid frames: the health bar flashes red when you start to pull threat. It's part of |cffffffffThreat Glow|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buffs & Debuffs|r\n• |cffffffffTimer Colour|r (on) is back as its own switch, in two places:\n      - Buffs & Debuffs (your buff and debuff frames).\n      - Unit Frames (auras on your frames).\n      - Turn it off to keep timers white.\n• Weapon enchants now start your first buff row instead of sitting in a row of their own. They count toward |cffffffffMax Icons|r.\n• The player frame shows your weapon enchants at the start of its buff row too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffFrame Style|r, first in the Frame section:\n      - |cffffffffBlizzard:|r Blizzard's strips, with no background or border.\n      - |cffffffffFlareUI|r (default): the strips on FlareUI's frame.\n      - |cffffffffCustom:|r no strips, with your own background and border.\n• |cffffffffQuest Buttons|r replaces Quest Icons and Voice Buttons. Pick |cffffffffNone|r, or tick |cffffffffQuest Icon|r, |cffffffffFocus Button|r and |cffffffffVoice Button|r. Your choices carry over.\n      - |cffffffffFocus Button|r brings back the small focus dot. Quest Icon and Focus Button can't both be on.\n      - |cffffffffVoice Button|r moved to the right end of the quest title, with Play, Stop and Replay.\n• Blizzard's glows: objectives glow when they move forward or finish, and quest titles glow when you accept or turn in a quest.\n• With Questie, focusing a quest while the world map is open flashes the quest on the map.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffBorder|r for the square minimap: |cffffffffBronze (Clean)|r (default), |cffffffffBronze (Header)|r, |cffffffffFlareUI Thick|r or |cffffffffFlareUI Thin|r.\n      - |cffffffffStyle|r is now just |cffffffffSquare|r or |cffffffffRound|r. Square (Header) carries over as |cffffffffBronze (Header)|r.\n• Edge icons: the sundial, Group Finder, Vehicle Exit and Durability icons slide along the map's edge, like addon buttons.\n      - Shift+drag to move one, Ctrl+mouse wheel to resize it, Shift+right-click or Ctrl+right-click to reset it.\n      - In Edit Mode, drag, scroll and right-click without holding a key.\n      - |cffffffffReset Minimap Icons|r, in Map Tools, puts them all back.\n• Info Bar: |cffffffffCoords (Simple)|r shows whole numbers, like 45, 62. The old choice is now |cffffffffCoords (Decimals)|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat, Meters and Quest Tracker|r\n• New border: |cffffffffFlareUI Frames Thick|r. The old border is now called |cffffffffFlareUI Frames Thin|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• |cffffffffTarget Mouseover|r (Off), in Options: opening a radial also targets the unit under your mouse.\n      - |cffffffffEnabled|r, or only while you hold |cffffffffShift|r, |cffffffffCtrl|r or |cffffffffAlt|r.\n      - Works in combat.\n• |cffffffffButton Names|r: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffOn Hover|r or |cffffffffAlways|r (was the Show Button Names switch).\n• About 220 more emotes.\n\n|cffe6cc99Tooltips|r\n• |cffffffffShow Guild Ranks|r (off) is back. It's greyed while |cffffffffShow Guild Name|r is off.\n• |cffffffffShow Faction|r (on) replaces Hide Faction. Your setting carries over.\n\n|cffe6cc99XP Bar|r\n• |cffffffffFlareUI XP Bar|r: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffSingle|r, |cffffffffSplit|r (default) or |cffffffffDouble|r (a second bar below the first).\n• |cffffffffXP Text|r is one dropdown: |cffffffffShow Always|r or |cffffffffShow On Mouseover|r, then tick |cffffffffPercent|r, |cffffffffValue|r, |cffffffffMax|r and |cffffffffRemaining|r. Your old choices carry over.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffZone Levels on the World Map|r (off), in Quality of Life › Map & Mail: a zone's level range under its name.\n• |cffffffff/kb|r opens Blizzard's Quick Keybind Mode, out of combat. If another addon already uses /kb, type |cffffffff/fui kb|r.\n• Gamepad: LB + D-pad moves between FlareUI's party and raid frames.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Bar Text: numbers in one spot show in the order you tick them. The menu shows 1, 2, 3 next to your ticks.\n• Tooltips: the Mouseover section is now |cffffffffPosition|r, with |cffffffffTooltip Corner|r at the top.\n      - |cffffffffOffset X|r and |cffffffffOffset Y|r hide while |cffffffffMouseover|r is |cffffffffNone|r.\n• Tooltips, Content tab: |cffffffffShow PvP|r comes before |cffffffffShow Faction|r, and |cffffffffSimplified Item Stats|r is last.\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffAuto Accept Quests|r and |cffffffffAuto Turn-In Quests|r are two switches again (were |cffffffffAutomate Quests|r). Your setting carries over.\n• XP Bar: |cffffffffBubbles|r is now |cffffffffSeparators|r.\n• Profiles: |cffffffffReset FlareUI|r sits in its own |cffffffffAddon Reset|r section.\n• Unit Frames › Fonts: the Level font has no Size any more. It follows the name in Addon Style, and the level disc in the ring styles.\n• Chat and Meters: the |cffffffffFading in Edit Mode|r buttons are gone. Fading itself is still in Edit Mode.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffCustom Emote|r is gone. A saved one becomes the matching emote, or keeps working as typed text.\n• Quest Tracker: quest titles use Blizzard's yellow.\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffShow Complete Tag|r turns only \"(Complete)\" green. The quest name keeps its colour.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffMacro Text|r sits centred under the icon.\n• Action Bars: with |cffffffffSkin Action Bars|r, stance, pet and small buttons show as much of the icon as the main bars.\n• Action Bars: a softer glow on the buttons of items you're wearing.\n• Buff Reminders: casts the highest rank each group member can take. Members too low for any rank don't count.\n• Minimap: Info Bar cells grow with their font, and a Middle cell on its own sits in the centre.\n• Pet frame: |cffffffffPower Height|r starts at 8, so the pet's resource bar shows. By AreChen.\n• Edit Mode is much faster: |cffffffffReset Settings|r, opening Edit Mode, dragging sliders and nudging with the arrow keys.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit frames: \"Dead\", \"Offline\" and \"Ghost\" no longer sit on top of the name.\n• Unit frames: a /reload during a cast no longer loses unit frames.\n• Tooltips: with |cffffffffHealth Bar|r set to |cffffffffInside|r, the bar no longer covers the last line (like PvP). When the game doesn't allow the room, the bar shows below the tooltip.\n• Buff Reminders: clicking skips group members who are out of range.\n• Chat: party, raid, guild and channel messages bring a faded chat back, like say and whispers.\n• Quest Tracker: tracking or untracking a quest in a fight waits until the fight ends, with no more blocked-action error.\n• Minimap: other addons' buttons outside the drawer sit above the border.\n• Addon drawer: an icon without a label is listed by its addon's name, not its live text.\n• Vendors: Shift+click to buy several items works again.\n• Delete Junk When Full works on the first loot window after logging in.\n• Loot Feed: money shows its coin icon.\n• FlareUI Style: glows pulse together.\n• Swing timer: the |cffffffffStand-Still Zone|r colour updates as soon as you change it.\n• Action Bars: pet command highlights show on skinned bars. By AreChen.\n• Sync Blizz UI keeps your bag sort settings at logout. By Nico-Mayer.\n• Radial editor: |cffffffffUndo Changes|r brings back your groups.\n• Setup tour: the reload button hides during a fight.\n• Settings: NEW tags no longer cover the text on button rows.\n\n|cffffd100Translations|r\n• Chinese (Simplified and Traditional): updated. By AreChen.\n• French: the 6.11 text. By Braincell1980." },
    { version = "6.11", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nThis is the biggest patch yet. Put any text on any side of your bars, give the minimap an Info Bar, pick your action bar and XP bar colours, hide the auras you never want to see, and get flag carrier frames that look like the rest of your UI. Plus a long list of things you asked for on Discord. Grab a drink: the list below is long.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffBuffs and debuffs:|r each frame now shows a set number: 6 (8 in Addon Style; 4 on focus, party and boss frames; 3 on the pet). Wide frames used to show more. Raise |cffffffffBuff Amount|r and |cffffffffDebuff Amount|r in each frame's Edit Mode settings.\n• |cffffffffTarget of Target and Target of Focus|r frames are on by default.\n• |cffffffffDefault font sizes|r changed on most unit frames (only if you never set them yourself):\n      - Player and target: 12 name, 12 health, 10 power.\n      - Focus and pet: 10, 10, 8.\n      - Target-of frames: 8, 8, 6.\n      - Raid: 10, 8, 6.\n      - Cast bars (all but the player's): 10.\n• |cffffffffFlip Portrait|r now moves the portrait to the other side of the frame instead of mirroring the picture. It's on (portrait on the right) by default.\n• |cffffffffOptions removed:|r\n      - |cffffffffStatus Colouring|r switch: pick the |cffffffffDisabled|r palette in |cffffffffStatus Colours|r instead.\n      - |cffffffffFull Player Names|r: pick |cffffffffFirst Name|r or |cffffffffFull Name|r in the bars' |cffffffffHealth Text|r.\n      - |cffffffffPortrait Size|r (FlareUI Style): the ring now grows with the frame's height.\n      - Minimap |cffffffffFramerate|r, |cffffffffLatency|r and |cffffffffCoordinates|r: they're now Info Bar cells.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffBar Text:|r put the name, health, power and level on the left, middle or right of each bar.\n• |cffffffffMinimap Info Bar:|r gold, bags, durability, framerate, latency or coordinates on the map. By Celbrund (GregDuhamel).\n• |cffffffffHide Auras:|r hide any buff or debuff on any frame.\n• |cffffffffColours:|r pick your own action bar status colours and XP bar colours.\n• |cffffffffFlag Carrier Frames:|r rebuilt in your frame style, with cast bars.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBar Text|r, in each frame's Edit Mode settings: |cffffffffHealth Text|r, |cffffffffPower Text|r and |cffffffffDruid Mana Text|r.\n      - Each has Left, Middle and Right spots. Tick what goes in each one.\n      - Health: First Name, Full Name, Health Percent, Health Value, Health Max, Health Lost.\n      - Power: Power Percent, Power Value, Power Max.\n      - Several items in one spot are split by \" / \".\n      - On the player, target, focus, pet and target-of frames, and the Resource Bars' health, power and druid mana bars.\n• |cffffffffShow Name|r (on), above |cffffffffShow Level|r, on every unit frame, party, raid and boss frame.\n• |cffffffffBuff Amount|r and |cffffffffDebuff Amount|r (1 to 12), under Buff Size and Debuff Size: how many show.\n      - On the unit frames, and on the party and boss frames when their auras sit above or below the frame.\n• |cffffffffShow Speed|r and |cffffffffHide Speed|r in the Fading section of the player, pet, target, focus and target-of frames. They start at Instant.\n• |cffffffffDamage Trail|r (on), under |cffffffffBar Edge Glow|r: turn off the light strip that shows the health you just lost.\n• |cffffffffThreat Glow|r and |cffffffffCombat Glow|r (on), in the Look section, after Class Colours.\n• Target of Target and Target of Focus: |cffffffffMirror Bars|r (on) and |cffffffffFlip Portrait|r (on).\n• Cast bars: |cffffffffBackground|r slider in every frame style.\n• Forever Style:\n      - |cffffffffPower Height|r: moves the line between health and power. The lowest step hides the power bar.\n      - |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r: in Cat or Bear Form the power bar splits in two, with your mana in the lower half.\n      - Power Text: |cffffffff> Value|r and |cffffffff> Percent|r put the number at the bar's right end, as on Blizzard's frame.\n      - Another player's name box takes their class colour while the frame's |cffffffffClass Colours|r is on.\n      - |cffffffffDispel Highlight|r: the plate's border lights up in the debuff's colour.\n• Far-higher mobs and bosses show the skull on the level, as on Blizzard's frames.\n\n|cffe6cc99Party, Raid and Boss Frames|r\n• Party: |cffffffffShow When Solo|r (off): your own party frame shows when you're not in a group. Needs |cffffffffShow Player|r.\n• Party and raid: |cffffffffPvP Flag|r icon (off), in the Icons section: the member's faction crest while flagged.\n• Raid: |cffffffffHide Player Frame in a Raid|r (off): your player and pet frames hide in a raid.\n• Boss frames, Addon Style: |cffffffffElite & Rare|r icon (on), in the Icons section.\n• With |cffffffffHide Player Frame in a Party|r on, your pet's happiness shows on your pet's party frame.\n\n|cffe6cc99Flag Carrier Frames|r\n• Rebuilt as FlareUI frames in your frame style: name, health, power, class portrait and a big faction crest.\n• |cffffffffCast bar|r (on).\n• Left-click targets the carrier, right-click sets your focus, as on Blizzard's frames.\n• |cffffffffFlip Portrait|r and |cffffffffMirror Bars|r (on), and their own fonts in Unit Frames › Fonts.\n• They show nothing Blizzard's frames don't: no range fading, no raid markers.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buffs & Debuffs|r\n• |cffffffffHide Auras|r tab: hide any aura on any frame.\n      - Pick one of your buffs or debuffs, or add one by its spell ID.\n      - Each hidden aura has a |cffffffffHide On|r list: Buffs & Debuffs, Player, Pet, Target, Focus, Party, Raid, Boss.\n      - The game lets addons hide buffs on you, your pet and your group, and debuffs on enemies. Debuffs on you or a friend only hide for a few spells, such as Sated.\n• Edit Mode: the Buffs sample shows the weapon enchant row too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffStatus Colours|r button, in Bars Appearance: pick the colours for Out of Range, Out of Mana, Unusable and On Cooldown.\n      - Palettes: FlareUI, Blizzard, |cffffffffDisabled|r (the game's own colours) or your own.\n      - The opacity slider sets how strong each colour is. On Cooldown at 0 means no dimming.\n• |cffffffffEquipped Item Border|r (off), after Show Button Art: the button of an item you're wearing gets a border in its quality colour.\n• |cffffffffXP Bar Colours|r button, at the bottom of Other Bars › XP Bar: XP, Rested XP, Rested Bonus, Quest XP, every reputation standing, Renown and Honor.\n• Bag buttons bar: |cffffffffSmaller Size|r (Off), in its Edit Mode settings: 50% to 70%, below Blizzard's smallest Size.\n• Combo Points bar (Resource Bars): |cffffffffStyle|r in Edit Mode: |cffffffffClassic|r gems or the |cffffffffModern|r bar, in any frame style.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Bar|r: up to three cells along the bottom of the square map: |cffffffffLeft|r, |cffffffffCenter|r, |cffffffffRight|r. By Celbrund (GregDuhamel).\n      - Each shows Gold, Bags, Durability, Framerate, Latency or Coordinates.\n      - |cffffffffShow Box|r (on) and |cffffffffOn Mouseover|r (off). Its own font in Minimap › Fonts.\n      - Round minimap: the Center cell, inside the circle.\n• |cffffffffFPS/Ping on Clock|r, in Map Tools: framerate and latency on the clock's tooltip.\n• |cffffffffVehicle Exit Button|r (off): Blizzard's exit arrow as a round icon on the map's edge.\n• |cffffffffDurability Warning|r (off): a repair icon on the map's edge, yellow or red as your gear wears down.\n• |cffffffffSundial Icon|r (on): turn the day and night badge off.\n• |cffffffffDrawer Style|r, first in Addon Buttons: |cffffffffDisabled|r, |cffffffffSundial|r or |cffffffffBlizzard|r (a button under the calendar).\n• |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r and fade groups for the minimap. Its icons hide while it's faded.\n• Round minimap: the Group Finder, Vehicle Exit and Durability icons sit around the circle's lower left.\n\n|cffe6cc99Tooltips|r\n• |cffffffffShow PvP|r (on), in Tweaks: the \"PvP\" line on flagged players and creatures is back.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• New |cffffffffSystems|r tab, with Camera and Gamepad.\n• |cffffffffCraft Batch Time|r (off), in Gameplay › Convenience: the cast bar also shows the time left for the whole batch.\n• |cffffffffAccept Summons|r (off), in Convenience: takes a summon for you after 10 seconds. A small window lets you cancel or go at once.\n• |cffffffffCombat Friendly Plates|r (off), in Nameplates: friendly players' nameplates show only during a fight.\n• |cffffffffUI Scale|r: a new scale asks you to keep it, and goes back after 15 seconds if you don't. |cffffd100/fui scale reset|r puts it back to the game's own.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffCombat Text Size|r, under Combat Text Font in General › Interface.\n• |cffffffffFlareUI Button|r (off), in General › ESC Menu: a FlareUI button in the game menu.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffRemind Before It Ends|r also offers 15, 30 and 45 seconds.\n• Bags: |cffffffffBoE Text|r (off): items that bind when equipped show BoE until bound.\n• Bags: |cffffffffPlain Empty Slots|r (off): every empty slot in the combined backpack looks the same.\n• Radial editor: spell tooltips show the rank, and pet spells are listed at the end of Spells.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Edit Mode:\n      - Switches sit in two columns.\n      - Cast bar sections share one order: Position, Bar Texture, Border Texture, Background, Height, Show Icon, Show Spell Timer, Show Spell Pushback.\n      - The Player Cast Bar's own section is now |cffffffffBehaviour|r.\n      - Width and Height sliders move in steps of 1. Your sizes stay as they are.\n      - Percent sliders show plain numbers, so \"100\" fits its box.\n      - |cffffffffOff|r is the first choice in every dropdown.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffStatus Colouring|r never dims a button for the global cooldown, so wand shots no longer grey the whole bar.\n• Action Bars: a button on cooldown is 25% grey by default, so its colour still shows.\n• Unit frames: the level uses the name's size in Addon Style.\n• Raid frames: |cffffffffPower Height|r defaults to 10.\n• Default positions and sizes in FlareUI Style and Forever Style: focus, pet, target-of frames, totems and flag carriers.\n• Addon Style: party frames' role icon sits bottom left; the pet's happiness face sits right of the frame.\n• General page: tabs are |cffffffffGeneral|r (with ESC Menu on top) and |cffffffffInterface|r.\n• Quality of Life: Other is now |cffffffffConvenience|r; Map & Mail sits above it in Gameplay.\n• Quest tracker with a gamepad: the right stick scrolls only after you click the tracker.\n• Loot rolls: tighter padding, and the header matches the chat's and the meter's. By Nico-Mayer.\n• French translation updated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action Bars: keybind text shows right after logging in, on every bar.\n• Action Bars: stance and pet buttons no longer show a second border inside FlareUI's.\n• Action Bars: no more Lua errors from the gamepad action bars.\n• Round minimap: quest areas no longer draw past the circle.\n• Quest Tracker: elite quests show their |cffffffff+|r again.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffBar Edge Glow|r no longer shows on a full health bar.\n• Forever Style: the portrait ring no longer bends when Power Height changes.\n• Edit Mode: the boss frames' sample buffs show right after a reload." },
}
